From: Wei Yongjun <weiyj.lk-Re5JQEeQqe8AvxtiuMwx3w@public.gmane.org>
Subject: [PATCH -next] spi: bcm-qspi: Remove unnecessary platform_set_drvdata()
Date: Thu,  9 Feb 2017 15:32:21 +0000
Message-ID: <20170209153221.2698-1-weiyj.lk@gmail.com>
Mime-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=ISO-8859-1
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
Cc: Wei Yongjun <weiyongjun1-hv44wF8Li93QT0dZR+AlfA@public.gmane.org>, linux-spi-u79uwXL29TY76Z2rM5mHXA@public.gmane.org
To: Mark Brown <broonie-DgEjT+Ai2ygdnm+yROfE0A@public.gmane.org>
Return-path: <linux-spi-owner-u79uwXL29TY76Z2rM5mHXA@public.gmane.org>
Sender: linux-spi-owner-u79uwXL29TY76Z2rM5mHXA@public.gmane.org
List-ID: <linux-spi.vger.kernel.org>

From: Wei Yongjun <weiyongjun1-hv44wF8Li93QT0dZR+AlfA@public.gmane.org>

The driver core clears the driver data to NULL after device_release
or on probe failure. Thus, it is not needed to manually clear the
device driver data to NULL.

Signed-off-by: Wei Yongjun <weiyongjun1-hv44wF8Li93QT0dZR+AlfA@public.gmane.org>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-bcm-qspi.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-bcm-qspi.c b/drivers/spi/spi-bcm-qspi.c
index 227096a..b3745d4 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-bcm-qspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-bcm-qspi.c
@@ -1399,7 +1399,6 @@ int bcm_qspi_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct bcm_qspi *qspi = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
-	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, NULL);
 	bcm_qspi_hw_uninit(qspi);
 	clk_disable_unprepare(qspi->clk);
 	kfree(qspi->dev_ids);



